":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229744,"global_rank":113216},{"name":"WittyAgnomen/political_bias","owner":"WittyAgnomen","html_url":"https://github.com/WittyAgnomen/political_bias","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"holds code for political bias paper","topics":[],"score":229740,"global_rank":113221},{"name":"nightlessbaron/TwitterGeoLoc","owner":"nightlessbaron","html_url":"https://github.com/nightlessbaron/TwitterGeoLoc","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"TwitterGeoLoc: An easy to use GeoTagging Tool","topics":["carmen","geolocation","twitter"],"score":229739,"global_rank":113224},{"name":"DefenseStorm/insightvmScanResults","owner":"DefenseStorm","html_url":"https://github.com/DefenseStorm/insightvmScanResults","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":3,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"DVM Integration for insightVM scan results reports","topics":[],"score":229736,"global_rank":113226},{"name":"bayesianbrad/blockchain-webapp","owner":"bayesianbrad","html_url":"https://github.com/bayesianbrad/blockchain-webapp","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A simple blockchain web application using the basic concepts.","topics":[],"score":229727,"global_rank":113231},{"name":"SiriRaavi/steering_angle_prediction